ted in theater and stage  productions and a little bit of drama  and i had taken a break for that to do  some comedy some multi-cam half-hour  stuff  uh so be being able to revisit that uh  for the first time in a while  it was really special to me and i just  love being able to  delve in with these emotional characters  and these emotional scenes  the road sequence was one i loved uh the  conversation between sean and will  at the stage um and  obviously some of the stuff with avery  yeah  he's like some of the stuff with bayley  not all of it  some of it was pretty good it was fine  well it's the dramatic stuff did you  guys  have instant chemistry because you can  see it on film was it something that  when you met  you guys just started laughing and  having a good time or did it build while  you were on set  yeah i mean i had met kevin uh years  prior actually  so uh we had met each other when we were  kind of you know babies and so getting  to  step into this world was so exciting to  kind of see each other and now be like  oh my gosh like we're adults now  like we love each other in this movie  and like you know we're gonna have to  like  you know so much of it was so different  and so fun but um  i would say you know our our whole cast  truly did become so close i mean we we  still talk to this day and  uh my bestie in the movie you know cat  she's like we talk all the time and  i think just every single day especially  four weeks of dance rehearsals when  we're all  thrown into such an unfamiliar  environment and we all had to lean on  each other i mean that's  that's destined to kind of you know  force you to create that that chemistry  and that love within each other so  there was a whole lot of trust and a lot  of inside jokes and a lot of giggles and  we had a great time  yeah the coolest parts of the film was  just the chemistry not only between  avery and will  which i was so excited to develop with  bayley uh with this film  uh but just the chemistry between all  the characters they all have  independent relationships with each  other and each relationship has a  different dynamic  and in a way we kind of fall in love  with the five characters as a whole  as much as we fall in love with each one  of them and  it's really hard to accomplish that in a  film i got to give it up to our casting  director beverly holloway too she did a  really nice job  putting that together
 

